## Part A (KD-2026-08-30c fix) — re-verified real, boundaries clean

Re-ran my attempt-1 fixture (refund-only HI row, no coverage overlap)
against the real router: Total renders $150.00, Per Month renders the
&mdash; placeholder + "no coverage in this range" text, never "0.00"; vs-Avg
column renders &mdash; for the row, no stray "%</td>". Fix is real.

Boundary probes (all built as HTTP tests against setupTestEnv fixtures,
dynamically asserted, not hand-predicted):
- coverageStart == segEnd (last day of range): NOT flagged no-coverage,
  renders a real dollar figure. Correct (ClippedHealthcareMonths uses
  `.After`, not `>=`, so equality counts as covered).
- coverageStart == segStart: NOT flagged no-coverage. Correct.
- Range entirely before coverage, zero HI rows in range: flagged
  no-coverage (dash), not $0.00. Correct — "no coverage" takes precedence
  over "coincidentally zero rows."
- hasCoverage true via an EARLIER premium outside the probed range (coverage
  predates the range), zero HI rows inside the probed range: renders a real
  $0.00, NOT the dash. Correct — this is the "genuinely zero rate with zero
  rows" case the ruling explicitly permits to render $0.00.
- Living kind: template's $noCoverage local is gated `and (eq .Type
  "healthcare") ...`; grep confirms HealthcareNoCoverageInRange is read in
  exactly those two guarded spots and nowhere else in any template/handler
  — no leakage to other kinds.

